Subject: fmt: make throw_exception's noreturn destructor survive clang 18+
Why: clang 18+ ignores [[noreturn]] on defaulted functions, so the
     '[[noreturn]] ~throw_exception() = default;' workaround no longer
     convinces -Wreturn-type that 'default: fmt::throw_exception(...)'
     switch arms cannot fall through; with -Werror=return-type (project
     default) this breaks the build (first hits: PPUDisAsm.h,
     SPUThread.h on the NDK/android build). A user-provided body of
     __builtin_unreachable() restores the CFG guarantee, warning-free on
     clang and gcc.
Upstream-status: candidate

diff --git a/Utilities/StrFmt.h b/Utilities/StrFmt.h
index 6d9ea05..6e0182f 100644
--- a/Utilities/StrFmt.h
+++ b/Utilities/StrFmt.h
@@ -394,7 +394,10 @@ namespace fmt
 		}
 
 #if !defined(_MSC_VER) || defined(__clang__)
-		[[noreturn]] ~throw_exception() = default;
+		// A user-provided noreturn body (not '= default') is required for clang's
+		// -Wreturn-type CFG to treat the full-expression as noreturn (clang 18+
+		// ignores [[noreturn]] on defaulted functions).
+		[[noreturn]] ~throw_exception() { __builtin_unreachable(); }
 #endif
 	};
 
